.0** fps (work max 106 -> 22.9 ms, no frame over 34 ms), live 4 chibis 26.8 -> **30.0** (32.4 -> 24.4 ms, work max 47.7 -> 33.8, the 27 frames of 50 ms gone), siege wave 3 29.5 -> **30.0**, Black Market 33.2 -> 28.7 ms, HomeMart cursor move 31.6 -> 29.1 ms; every one of the 19 house windows 30.0 with no frame over two vblanks (`expect-fps 29.5` + `expect-gap 34` on the turn, the busy layout and Hold the Door); test-home `home_steady` 29.2 -> 30.0, `home_rotate` 24.5 -> 30.0 (their floors are 29.5 now; `expect-gap` no longer stops report-only runs). Tests: `room-parity` path 3 (every golden line 0..57 as a sliced turn, hashed against the one-go golden; a mutant that never slices fails), `home_turn.txt`, two core tests. GBA ROM +4,880 B, EWRAM and resident IWRAM unchanged (ledger row 47; the room group 3,588 -> 9,512 B inside the 3D group's slot, 840 B free). PS1: nothing changes (the EXE and the overlays are byte for byte the tip's, 72,736 B below the stack top with the boot FMV, delta 0 B), every house window 30.0-30.5 (the busy layout, 28.8 fps on the base, is 30.00 since PS1-FLAT landed); Dreamcast: all 19 windows under 33.3 ms, as before (work mean 3.4 ms, max 20.6 ms). **Still short:** the house entry (a 152 ms first frame and a 129 ms recompose the tick after, under the load fade: S3-10), the stress layouts `home_cellar_full` (26.0), `home_modal_busy` (25.0) and `home_defend_w3` (14.7), and the creator hat try-on named in the roadmap row (not touched).
